course: dictionary
lesson: 3463
title: Words from a fair
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A fairground is an open area where a fair is held. It has rides, games, stalls and food. When you meet this word, look at the words around it: they will tell you what kind of place is meant.
explain: «Fairground rides are checked often and are very safe.» Here fairground describes the rides, so it tells you they belong to a fair. Writers also use fairground in front of other words, such as «fairground games», to show what kind of games they mean.
explain: Use the swap test to check your meaning. «Fairground games are set up so the stall makes money.» Put in "an open area where a fair is held" and read it again. If the sentence still makes sense, your meaning is right.
fact: A fairground is an open area where a fair is held.
fact: Fairgrounds have rides, games, stalls and food.
fact: Fairground can also describe things from a fair, as in «fairground rides» and «fairground games».
fact: «Fairground rides are checked often and are very safe.»
fact: A fright on a ride can stay with you for weeks, even when the ride is safe.
exercise: What is a fairground? | *An open area where a fair is held, with rides, games and stalls | A farm where animals are sold | A quiet park with benches and a pond | A hall used only for school dances
exercise: In «fairground games», which word tells you the games belong to a fair? | *fairground | the | are | games
exercise: «Fairground games are set up so the stall makes money; most people lose.» What does this suggest? | The stall gives money away to everyone | *The games are set up to make money for the stall, so most players lose | Everyone who plays wins a big prize | The games are free and always fair to players
test: What does «fairground» mean in the phrase «fairground rides»? | *Belonging to a fair, such as rides at a fair | Belonging to a sports club, such as team rides | Belonging to a train station, such as platform rides | Belonging to a farm, such as tractor rides
test: «A fright like being stuck at the top can stick for weeks.» What is a fright? | *A sudden feeling of fear | A prize you win at a game | A kind of sweet | A ride that goes very fast
exam: Which sentence uses fairground to describe something, rather than naming a place? | We went to the fairground on Saturday | *The fairground rides were checked before the fair opened | The fairground was full of noise and lights | We ate candyfloss at the fairground
